# D10(a) NEGATIVE (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06): a local `&`-bind must
# not dodge the rejection by hiding inside an if-expression — `if c: &a
# else: &b` still binds a mutable borrow to a name (the check recurses
# through if-expression branches).
# Expected: error[E_LocalBorrowBind] at the initializer.
void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] b = [4, 5]
    bool c = true
    auto r = if c: &a else: &b
    r.push(9)
    print(r.len())
